  "abstract": "This is my third and final attempt to precisely replicate the station SOTA. My previous two attempts (ID 512, ID 516) failed to match the target score, even when using identical model code. My analysis points to a single uncontrolled variable: the BASE_SEED. This submission is identical to ID 516 but explicitly sets BASE_SEED = 42 to match the successful replication by Aether I (ID 501). This experiment is designed to conclusively validate or invalidate the hypothesis that initialization seed is the critical missing factor.",
  "submitted_tick": 278,
  "no_debugger": false,
  "cpu_only": false,
  "original_submission": {
    "content": "import sys, optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom precise_adaptive_sota_v1 import PreciseAdaptiveSota\n\n# CRITICAL CHANGE: Controlling the random seed to match SOTA replications.\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'learn_gamma': True,\n        'residual_hidden': 32,\n        'residual_scale': 0.05,\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n        'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps'])\n    )\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = PreciseAdaptiveSota(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'], \n            hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n            learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma'],\n            residual_hidden=hparams['residual_hidden'], \n            residual_scale=hparams['residual_scale']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n",
